<Base title="Launch Kit" description="Turn local artwork into inspected icons, PWA assets and social graphics, then deliberately apply them to an owned app."><h1>Make an identity you can use.</h1><p class="lede">Choose local artwork, prepare icons and a shared-link image, inspect the actual output files and download one portable package.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://composer-launch-kit.loftwah.workers.dev/">Open the independent editor</a><a class="button secondary" href="/init/launch-kit">Import a prepared package</a></div><p>Image preparation stays in your browser. The standalone editor needs no account. Composer adoption is a deliberate local import with review before use.</p><section><h2>From artwork to a working app.</h2><p>The fictional Night Signal package was exported from Launch Kit, checked through Composer’s import review and applied to an independent static listening timer. Open it, start a session and inspect the actual served icons, manifest and social image.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/launch-kit/example/">Try Night Signal</a><a href="https://share.loftwah.com/">Inspect with Link Check</a></div><p class="small">A served file check is separate from physical installation, native platform sharing and owner artistic acceptance.</p></section></Base>
